NNAAMMEE
     vviicc — VMware VMXnet Virtual Interface Controller device

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     vviicc** aatt ppccii??

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vviicc driver provides support for the VMXnet virtual NIC available in
     virtual machines by VMware.  It appears as a simple Ethernet device but
     is actually a virtual network interface to the underlying host operating
     system.

     This driver supports the vvmmxxnneett driver protocol, as an alternative to the
     emulated pcn(4) and em(4) interfaces also available in the VMware envi‐
     ronment.  The vviicc driver is optimized for the virtual machine, it can
     provide advanced capabilities depending on the underlying host operating
     system and the physical network interface controller of the host.

     The vviicc driver supports VMware virtual NICs provided by the following
     products:

           ••   VMware ESX 2.0 and newer
           ••   VMware GSX 2.5 and newer
           ••   VMware Server 1.0 and newer
           ••   VMware Workstation 4.5 and newer
           ••   VMware Fusion 1.0 and newer

     The vviicc driver supports the following media types:

     autoselect  Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                 driver always uses the fastest available speed and the media
                 options provided by the underlying host of the virtual ma‐
                 chine.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     The following entry must be added to the VMware configuration file to
     provide the vviicc device:

           ethernet0.virtualDev = "vmxnet"

